  "query_preview": "..\n(Tonight through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1149 PM CDT Tue Aug 4 2026\n\nClear skies prevail across the Mid-South as a weakening ridge\nbuilds in from the northwest. While a cutoff low over northeast\nGeorgia keeps the Deep South seasonably cool, the ridge has\nallowed temperatures to rebound locally. Dry conditions will\npersist across the Mid-South through at least midweek.\n\nHighs will climb into the low to mid-90s after Wednesday as\nsoutherly flow develops in response to the weakening cutoff low\nand deepening low pressure over the Southern Plains. This flow\nwill push dew points into the upper 70s by Thursday, driving heat\nindices into the triple digits. Portions of northwest Mississippi\nand east-central Arkansas, primarily south of Memphis, may\napproach Heat Advisory criteria (105F) on Thursday.\n\nA weak trough in northwest flow will increase rain and\nthunderstorm chances by Friday, though guidance limits PoPs to\naround 30%, with the highest coverage north of I-40. While this\nshortwave and associated cloud cover may slightly curb Saturday's\ntemperatures, elevated humidity will maintain triple-digit heat\nindices across much of the region.\n\nAs the trough shifts east, Sunday looks slightly drier and a\ndegree or two warmer, mainly due to the lack of clouds and\nprecipitation. The threat of Heat Advisory conditions will\npersist into early next week.",
